{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>The lamp of YHWH is the soul of man</b> — by way of parable, for the soul is drawn from His light, and its resting-place is the head, and from there it illuminates the spirit and the soul with its intellect, and it is illuminated by its light. Therefore it is called His lamp, as though He searches with it the chambers of the belly, and it is a hint to the heart, which is the chamber of thoughts." "Another interpretation: <b>The lamp of YHWH</b> — it alludes to the light of His intellect, that is, the lamp of Elohim searches the soul of man and searches every chamber of the belly. And HaShem, when He searches the heart of the king and knows what the heart of the wicked thinks, then He sends His kindness and truth to guard the king from distress, and HaShem sustains His throne, on account of the kindness that the king does."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:23:53.131607117Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}